  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Markets NiSCOPS2 2024-2028</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IDH and Solidaridad partnered to implement a second, five-year phase of the National Initiatives for Sustainable &amp; Climate-smart Oil-Palm Smallholders (NI-SCOPS), a flagship oilpalm production programme that is currently operating in partnership with the governments of Indonesia, Malaysia, Ghana, Nigeria, Colombia and the Netherlands. NI-SCOPS Phase II has an additional focus on influential market countries and regions, namely India and Asia, the United Kingdom (UK) and the European Union (EU), particularly in the context of the impact of the forthcoming EU Deforestation Regulation (EUDR 2023 1115). The program is designed to benefit approximately 110,000 SHFs. It includes scaling solutions for two of the main unintended consequences of EUDR 2023, namely segregation of the palm-oil supply chain at the expense of SHFs in countries deemed to be high risk, and further leakage of deforestation to African and Asian markets.</narrative>
  </description>
